{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791730413,"nonce":"04oW3nwOaf89eptTA3DScGEaqDg=","title":"CSS text-decoration","message":"Support text-decoration and its five longhands: which lines (underline, overline, line-through, several at once), style (solid, double, dotted, dashed), colour (the text's own or given) and thickness/offset (the font's own or given). Set on the element that declares it; a descendant's own decoration draws beside its ancestors', and none undoes them, as CSS does and as blinc_abi's decorations_of already draws (text-shadow's model). Drawing and parsing already existed in blinc_abi for blinc_ts's use; this adds the HashLink route (property 120) and a Haxe-side CSS compose handler that mirrors blinc_abi's own shorthand/longhand priority.","files":null}]}